The Facility Drain Coordinator source tree contains no third-party source
code. It builds and tests with a C++20 compiler and CMake alone, with no
network access and no downloaded dependencies. The only non-standard-library
interfaces it uses are operating-system facilities for file creation, file
replacement, file locking and cache flushing; those are provided by the host
operating system and are not distributed with this repository.

Facility Drain Coordinator does not collect or transmit any telemetry. Every
record it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never
leaves the machine running the software.

